# PART 1: 
## DATA FOUNDATION 

# 1. Original Data (Raw Operational Inputs)
These are the base fields captured from customer support activity:
Ticket ID
Created Date / Resolved Date
Agent
Category (e.g., Login Issue, Payment Problem)
Priority
Resolution Hours
CSAT Score (1–5)
Channel (Chat / Email / etc.)
Subscription Type (Free / Premium)
## Purpose:
Represents real operational ticket data
Used as the source for all analysis

2. Lookup Data (Enrichment Layer)
These fields were added to enrich the dataset:
Team (via agent mapping)
Location
Experience Level
SLA Target Hours (based on priority or SLA rules)
## Purpose:
Adds context for segmentation
Enables operational breakdown by team, agent, and service level

3. Business Logic Columns (Calculated Fields)
These columns convert raw data into measurable operations metrics:

# SLA Status
Measures operational performance against SLA targets

=IF([@[Resolution Hours]]<=[@[SLA Target Hours]],"Met SLA","Breached SLA")

# Resolution Category
Classifies ticket resolution speed

=IF([@[Resolution Hours]]<=2,"Fast",
IF([@[Resolution Hours]]<=5,"Medium","Slow"))

# CSAT Category
Converts numeric CSAT into customer experience segments

=IF([@[CSAT Score]]>=4,"Satisfied",
IF([@[CSAT Score]]=3,"Neutral","Unsatisfied"))


# Priority Group
Standardizes priority levels for analysis

=IF([@Priority]="High","High Priority",
IF([@Priority]="Medium","Medium Priority","Low Priority"))

# Customer Type
Enables segmentation between Free and Premium customers

=[@[Subscription Type]]

# Structured analytics model

✔ Operational data (tickets) 
✔ Enriched context (teams, SLA targets) 
✔ Business logic (SLA, CSAT, resolution speed) 
✔ Analytical segmentation (priority, customer type, categories)

## Analyst Insight

Measure operational efficiency (SLA performance)
Analyze customer experience (CSAT segmentation)
Identify bottlenecks (resolution categories)
Segment performance by customer type and priority

